+### Tenant session
+
+A user may belong to several entities (memberships) but works in **one at a time**: `session('current_entity_id')`. Only the HTTP layer reads it — the `current_entity` route middleware turns it into an in-request `App\Tenancy\TenantContext` and aborts `403` if the user is not a member of that entity. With an empty session: 0 memberships → onboarding (`/onboarding`, creates the first entity; the creator becomes its owner), 1 → the session is set automatically, more than 1 → entity switcher (`/e/switcher`; picking is audited on the `audit` log channel). `/home` dispatches the same way and lands on the entity dashboard. Permissions live in `EntityPolicy` / `EntityMembershipPolicy`: anyone authenticated may create an entity, any member may view it, owner and admin may update/delete it, only the owner manages settings; owner/admin assign roles; a membership can be removed by owner/admin or by its own user, never the owner's.
+
 **Invariants:**
 
 - Every entity has exactly one owner.
